# OpenRobOps configs

This folder contains YAML files that need to be applied to OpenRobOps to configure data sources, 
actions and other settings in OpenRobOps specific to this flatland simulation.

## Welcome page content

The Welcome dashboard uses seven text widgets across three sections:

**Intro section** (no title)

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-intro.md` | full width | Welcome heading and OpenRobOps intro |

**Dashboards section**

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-fleet.md` | 4 columns | Fleet dashboard description |
| `welcome-robot.md` | 4 columns | Robot dashboard description |
| `welcome-navigation.md` | 4 columns | Navigation dashboard description |

**Simulation section**

| File | Layout | Content |
|------|--------|---------|
| `welcome-simulation-map.md` | 6 columns | Simulation details and ASCII map |
| `welcome-action.md` | 6 columns | Commands and key-value telemetry |
| `welcome-footer.md` | full width | GitHub / docker environment link |

After editing any file, regenerate `config.yaml`:

```
node embed-welcome-content.mjs
```

## Apply configs

To apply configs, use InOrbit's CLI. First set up `INORBIT_CLI_API_KEY` and
`INORBIT_CLI_URL` (e.g. http://oro.example.com/api) environment variables, then:
```
inorbit apply -f config.yaml
```
